{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","roleHeading":"Protocol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L54"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"type":"inheritsFrom"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertices","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper that adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", can own any mutable directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation as its base through this protocol and work on it without extra hashing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertices.Index == Int"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedPseudograph"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition to ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s laws:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_key(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_vertex(atKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal the unprefixed members for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that vertex’s key becomes "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Otherwise it returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and no other key changes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, and traps on any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", returning the removed instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":", then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for each vertex in order, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for each pair"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in order. It gives the same graph and the same position for each pair."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", plus O(1) per live vertex. That matches the representation’s own page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"span can exceed the vertex count, because removals leave holes and a decoded graph may start at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any position. Its decoder bounds the span at ","type":"text"},{"code":"16 × vertexCount + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pages. Keys before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest live key cost nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" return the stored rows typed as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuccessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"PredecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the elements are positions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes. ","type":"text"},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not a requirement because its return type varies by representation.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position, and a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. Generic code inserts an edge by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The underscored members are for wrappers inside the library. Callers use the representations’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" members, which take vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"title":"DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(_:)":{"title":"remove(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Removes ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and every edge at it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"remove"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol"